#{[17592186459272 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186459143 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459272 #edb/ref 1069 "q-133645" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459272 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459272 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the degree of the polynomial that represents the area of John's plot of land?\n\nDegree $\\,=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459272 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b051d769-5fa1-57de-9369-1a061bff6200" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459272 #edb/ref 1074 "The polynomial \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+x-12\n$$\n\ncan be written as\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{x}^{1}-12{x}^{0}.\n$$\n\nSo, it has the exponents $2,$ $1,$ and $0.$ The degree is the largest of these exponents, which is $2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459295 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186459139 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459295 #edb/ref 1069 "q-133642" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459295 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459295 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/eb/ebd87e37a8f01369e1f62f166879d08a4d2e6cc59a787662a36ec0a297036878.png)\n\nBrenda is Dan's neighbor. She has a plot of land whose area is ${x}^{2}-4$ square yards and whose width is $x+2$ yards, as depicted above. What is the length of Brenda's plot in terms of $x?$\n\nBrenda's plot has a length of \n{{field-1}}\nyards." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459295 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "dcf83646-321d-5883-b39d-559061dc5018" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459295 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the length of Brenda's plot of land, we need to factor the expression ${x}^{2}-4.$\n\nFirst, we write the expression as a difference of squares:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-4={x}^{2}-{2}^{2}\n$$\n\nThen, we factor the expression using the difference of squares formula:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-{2}^{2}=(x+2)(x-2)\n$$\n\nAs a result, we conclude that the length of the plot must be $x-2$ yards.\n\n![](images/af/af8ec2bf60ee66fb71ad633dbcd5963bbb4aaa7f670cbfc76f4e2855021c1bf3.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459300 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186459120 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459300 #edb/ref 1069 "q-133646" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459300 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459300 #edb/ref 1071 "If $x=10\\,\\text{yd},$ what is the area of John's land plot?\n\nArea $\\,=$\n{{field-1}}\n${\\text{yd}}^{2}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459300 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "eedc1616-8911-59c0-a664-fbc46a72c752" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459300 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the area, we have to evaluate the polynomial ${x}^{2}+x-12$ at $x=10.$\n\nSo, we substitute $x=10$ into the polynomial and simplify: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+x-12 & = \\\\ (10)^{2}+(10)-12 & = \\\\ 100+10-12 & = \\\\ 98\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area is $98\\,{\\text{yd}}^{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459302 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186459150 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459302 #edb/ref 1069 "q-133647" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459302 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459302 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/f9/f9588aa7f0e8dd48c3f9cc334a63ee529fa95468b4461fb33441abfb13118233.png)\n\nWhen $x=10\\,\\text{yd},$ the dimensions of John's plot of land are $14\\,\\text{yd}$ and $7\\text{yd}.$ A water pipe goes diagonally from one corner to the opposite, as shown above. Find the **exact** length of the pipe.\n\nThe length of the pipe is \n{{field-1}}\nyards." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459302 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f44b4615-3a8f-5adb-80bf-fcc20a241638" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459302 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that we have a right triangle with legs $a=14\\,\\text{yd}$ and $b=7\\,\\text{yd}.$\n\n![](images/4b/4b28a9cd713d5098bb735236f3b9d96eaefaffb09a165a951bbbee56b25a1451.png)\n\nLet $c$ be the length of the hypotenuse. Then, according to the Pythagorean theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}^{2} & ={a}^{2}+{b}^{2} \\\\ c & =\\sqrt{{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the values for $a$ and $b$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =\\sqrt{{14}^{2}+{7}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{196+49} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{245}\\,\\text{yd}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459303 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186459128 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459303 #edb/ref 1069 "q-133648" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459303 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459303 #edb/ref 1071 "Dan purchased his land for $160$ thousand dollars. The value of the land increases by $10%$ each year. How much will Dan's plot be worth after $5$ years? Round your answer to the nearest thousand dollars.\n\nAfter $5$ years, the land will be worth approximately \n{{field-1}}\n thousand dollars." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459303 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f48bf863-db11-5ccc-aed1-6f7b1c30fa89" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459303 #edb/ref 1074 "The land initially costs $160$ thousand, which increases at a rate of $10%$ per year.\n\n$10%$ as a decimal is $0.1.$ Therefore, an increase of $10%$ corresponds to multiplication by a factor of\n\n$$\n1+0.1=1.1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n* After $1$ year, the value will be $160\\cdot (1.1)$ thousand dollars\n\n* After $2$ years, the value will be $160\\cdot (1.1)^{2}$ thousand dollars\n\n* After $3$ years, the value will be $160\\cdot (1.1)^{3}$ thousand dollars\n\n* After $4$ years, the value will be $160\\cdot (1.1)^{4}$ thousand dollars\n\n* After $5$ years, the value will be $160\\cdot (1.1)^{5}$ thousand dollars\n\nEvaluating the expression for the value after $5$ years, we get the following:\n\n$$\n160\\cdot (1.1)^{5}=257.68≈258\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.\n\nTherefore, after $5$ years, the land will be worth approximately $258$ thousand dollars." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459311 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186459325 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459311 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "04c07f5e-ec05-58c1-a73d-161afe6f7ad7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459311 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186459268 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459316 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "225da2fe-dd6e-5dd3-9370-09c5445ce257" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459316 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186459203 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459317 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186459328 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459317 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "30ea2726-c12a-571d-9af1-d4e0091dda3f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459317 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186459302 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459318 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "327a0400-0c63-5f30-a3ce-362aa4e3cb09" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459318 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186459209 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459320 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186459333 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459320 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "348df397-ddb1-51a5-a4c4-9a07ca6576dc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459320 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186459231 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459325 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186459340 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459325 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5d669dc7-65f8-57af-ba32-ad858e971581" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459325 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186459240 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459328 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186459318 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459328 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8c735fea-50f8-5379-bf22-9c22e55108f8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459328 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186459303 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459329 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186459317 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459329 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "90ffdeae-e5b0-50bb-a735-bc07d89b8df1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459329 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186459300 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459333 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186459311 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459333 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c7cec136-4393-5919-92ac-4e6e09cd3a11" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459333 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186459295 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459340 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186459329 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459340 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "fdf93b38-11ec-5574-967b-14c1df602df6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459340 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186459272 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
